; The stress, first part. A rules word's phonemes (10 x code) are kept in cells 80-95, noting whether one is a vowel
; other than AX (below 180). At its end (-21, or -22 for a function word) out go that card, ah (1 when the word has
; no vowel but AX), the phonemes with the last as -100 - it, then -20, for posth. Anything else goes through as it
; is, phonemes before it first. Phonemes past the 16th are dropped.
;
; Address Contents Label Opcode Operand Comment
  03            rec     INP   x        03-23: a phoneme is kept; is it a vowel other than AX
  04                    CLA   x
  05                    TAC   end
  06                    SUB   c180
  07                    TAC   vow
  08                    JMP   kp
  09            vow     CLA   z
  10                    STO   ah
  11            kp      CLA   n
  12                    SUB   n16
  13                    TAC   st
  14                    JMP   rec
  15            st      CLA   s80
  16                    ADD   n
  17                    STO   wr
  18                    CLA   x
  19            wr      DATA  0        (STO 80 + n)
  20                    CLA   n
  21                    ADD   00
  22                    STO   n
  23                    JMP   rec
  24            end     CLA   n16      24-37: a rules word: its end card and ah first, the last phoneme marked
  25                    STO   last
  26                    CLA   x
  27                    SUB   m20
  28                    TAC   word
  29                    JMP   out
  30            word    OUT   x
  31                    OUT   ah
  32                    CLA   n
  33                    SUB   00
  34                    STO   last
  35                    CLA   m20
  36                    STO   x
  37            out     CLA   z        37-63: the phonemes, then the end card
  38                    STO   i
  39            lp      CLA   i
  40                    SUB   n
  41                    TAC   one
  42                    OUT   x
  43                    CLA   z
  44                    STO   n
  45                    CLA   00
  46                    STO   ah
  47                    JMP   rec
  48            one     CLA   c80
  49                    ADD   i
  50                    STO   rd
  51            rd      DATA  0        (CLA 80 + i)
  52                    STO   y
  53                    CLA   i
  54                    SUB   last
  55                    TAC   put
  56                    CLA   m100
  57                    SUB   y
  58                    STO   y
  59            put     OUT   y
  60                    CLA   i
  61                    ADD   00
  62                    STO   i
  63                    JMP   lp
  64            x       DATA  0
  65            n       DATA  0
  66            ah      DATA  1
  67            last    DATA  0
  68            i       DATA  0
  69            y       DATA  0
  70            z       DATA  0
  71            c180    DATA  180
  72            n16     DATA  16
  73            m20     DATA  -20
  74            m100    DATA  -100
  75            s80     STO   80
  76            c80     CLA   80
